## skills/grillme, skills/handoff, skills/wait-what

Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock
Source: https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
License: MIT (full text in LICENSE-mattpocock-skills)

`wait-what` is bundled verbatim.

`grillme` is adapted from his `grill-me` and `grilling`. Upstream, `grill-me` is
a one-line stub that hands off to `grilling`, so the two only work as a pair.
Here they are one self-contained file, renamed to match the `/grillme` that
Your AI Dept.'s handouts teach. The Your AI Dept. changes, none of them
upstream: a cap of twelve questions per session, questions asked in plain
English, and a closing summary of the agreed plan.

`handoff` is adapted from his `handoff`. The Your AI Dept. changes: it saves
`HANDOFF.md` in the working folder instead of the OS temp directory, and it ends
by telling the user what to type in a fresh session.

Upstream sets both to `disable-model-invocation`. Here neither is, so a request
made mid-message ("then run /grillme") still reaches them.

The upstream repo is the canonical version and gets updates first. Pull from
there if you want to track changes, and re-apply the changes above if you do.

